# Milestone: M3
# Covers: Semaphore.criticalSection(fn) as an alternative to acquire/release;
#         same ordered-wakeup semantics as basic.chk but via the helper method.
# defer-to: M6 (requires Semaphore stdlib type and criticalSection method)
#
# Reason:
#   Semaphore and its criticalSection() helper method are stdlib features scheduled
#   for M6.  The fixture is functionally identical to semaphore/basic.chk but
#   exercises the criticalSection() helper API path.  Will be activated together
#   with basic.chk when M6 lands.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M6 with Semaphore type and M5 chk driver):
# # var s = Semaphore.new(0) | {};
# # function f(name) { ... s.criticalSection(function() { sleep(1s) }) } | {};
# # f("func1"), ... s.release(); ...
# # (see legacy/repos/aldebaran-urbi/tests/2.x/semaphore/critical.chk)
